          "title": "Variables and Scope Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. var, let, const",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "var",
                "let",
                "const"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "function",
                  "block",
                  "block"
                ],
                [
                  "Reassign",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A block is any ==`{ }`==: `if`, `for`, or a bare block",
                "`const` locks the ==binding==, not the value"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const a = [];",
                "a.push(1);  // works",
                "a = [];     // TypeError"
              ],
              "note": "mutating is fine, rebinding throws"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lexical scope and lookup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Lexical== = visibility fixed by where code is **written**",
                "Not by where the function is **called**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Current scope",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Enclosing scopes",
                    "sub": "outward",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ReferenceError",
                    "sub": "not found",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Global object",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Global declaration",
                "On globalThis?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`var`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "function declaration",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`let` / `const`",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Top-level `let x = 1` gives `globalThis.x` as ==undefined==; only `var` and functions attach."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hoisting and the Temporal Dead Zone",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Hoisting and the Temporal Dead Zone",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What hoisting does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Hoisting==: declarations are registered at scope creation, before code runs",
                "The name exists from the **top of its scope**",
                "`var` is hoisted and initialised to ==undefined=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "console.log(x);",
                "var x = 5;"
              ],
              "note": "no error: x exists, value undefined"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "undefined"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. let, const and functions",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`let`/`const` are hoisted but **uninitialised**",
                "Access before the declaration line → {red:ReferenceError}",
                "That gap is the ==TDZ== (temporal dead zone)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Used before its line",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`var x`",
                  "`undefined`"
                ],
                [
                  "`let` / `const`",
                  "{red:ReferenceError}"
                ],
                [
                  "function declaration",
                  "works, body hoisted"
                ],
                [
                  "`var f = function(){}`",
                  "{red:TypeError}: not a function"
                ],
                [
                  "`typeof` on TDZ variable",
                  "{red:ReferenceError}"
                ],
                [
                  "`typeof` on undeclared name",
                  "`'undefined'`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Does let hoist?** Yes, but it stays in the TDZ until its line runs",
                "**Why TypeError on an early call?** `var f` is undefined, not a function",
                "**typeof on a TDZ variable?** Throws; an undeclared name gives 'undefined'"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Closures: How They Work and Where to Use Them",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Closures: How They Work and Where to Use Them",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a closure is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Closure== = function + reference to the scope where it was created",
                "Keeps that scope **alive** after the outer function returns",
                "Captures by ==reference==, not value: later changes are seen"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Private state and factories",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`n` is private: only the returned function can touch it",
                "Factory: outer arg fixed now, inner arg later (==partial application==)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function counter(){ let n = 0; return () => ++n }",
                "const c = counter();",
                "console.log(c(), c());",
                "function mul(a){ return b => a*b }",
                "const double = mul(2);",
                "console.log(double(5), c.n);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1 2",
                "10 undefined"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common uses",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Use",
                "Closure remembers"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Callbacks, event handlers",
                  "the data they need"
                ],
                [
                  "Memoisation",
                  "the cache object"
                ],
                [
                  "`once` / `debounce`",
                  "a called flag / timer id"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Shared, not copied",
              "text": "The inner function reads the **live** variable. Change it outside and the closure sees the ==new value=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Loop Closure Pitfall",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Loop Closure Pitfall",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Bug",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "All callbacks share ==one function-scoped `i`==",
                "Callbacks run later, after the loop ends, when `i` is 3"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {",
                "  setTimeout(() => console.log(i))",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "3",
                "3",
                "3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three Fixes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fix",
                "How",
                "Prints"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`let` in loop head",
                  "fresh binding copy per iteration",
                  "0 1 2"
                ],
                [
                  "IIFE (legacy)",
                  "`(function(j){ setTimeout(()=>console.log(j)) })(i)`",
                  "0 1 2"
                ],
                [
                  "`forEach` / `map`",
                  "callback parameter is a new scope per element",
                  "0 1 2"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Same Trap: Click Handlers",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Handlers attached in a `var` loop all read the ==final index==",
                "Fix the same way: `let` or an IIFE"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why 3 3 3?** One shared `i`, already 3 when callbacks run",
                "**Why does `let` fix it?** Each iteration gets its own binding copy"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`var` = one shared binding; `let` in the loop head = ==one binding per iteration=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "IIFE and Modules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "IIFE and Modules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. IIFE and module pattern",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`(function(){ ... })();` ==runs once==, private scope",
                "Wrapping `( )` make it an ==expression==, not a declaration",
                "Module pattern: IIFE returns ==public methods==; vars stay private via **closures**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const counter = (function () {",
                "  let n = 0;",
                "  return { inc: () => ++n };",
                "})();",
                "counter.inc(); // n is unreachable"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ES modules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Own ==module scope==: top-level vars are **not global**",
                "{blue:Strict mode} by default",
                "Loaded ==once==, then cached",
                "Exports are ==live bindings==: importers see new values of an exported `let`",
                "Importers **cannot assign** to an import"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "// a.js",
                "export let count = 0;",
                "export function inc() { count++; }",
                "// b.js",
                "import { count, inc } from './a.js';",
                "inc();        // count is now 1",
                "count = 5;    // TypeError"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. What to use",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Use",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "IIFE",
                  "old script-tag code"
                ],
                [
                  "ES modules",
                  "new code"
                ],
                [
                  "`const`",
                  "default"
                ],
                [
                  "`let`",
                  "when reassigning"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:`var`}",
                  "never"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
